{
 "enum": "SpellEffect.Effect slot typing",
 "description": "What each effect value's misc columns hold on the rows it selects: a reference into a table, a vocabulary or mask a vendored vocabulary names, an amount, a scripted argument, or unread by the server. Read mechanically, never by hand, so it can be held against the build's own payloads: `by` names the evidence. declared is not used here; measured means the slot's distinct values resolve into one id space far beyond the space's density over their range; named means the selector's name points at the table and the values fit it; core means the Epsilon core's handler reads the value as that vocabulary, or, for unread, that neither the handler nor any read of the aura in the core asks for it; scripted means the number is an argument the spell's own server script reads; shaped means an amount by name or by round values. A slot no evidence types is listed under unresolved. family is the selector's RP family, the ranking's axis.",
 "source": [
  "the 9.2.7 SpellEffect rows, the id spaces of every table the exploration database holds, the Epsilon core's SpellAuraEffects.cpp and SpellEffects.cpp",
  "https://github.com/EpsilonRP/TrinityCore"
